# **Knight Lore — Core Architecture & Gameplay Logic Specification (Godot Reimplementation)**

This specification is extracted from the ZX Spectrum Z80 disassembly of *Knight Lore* (1984) and is structured for direct use in a Godot 4 reimplementation.

## **1\. Coordinate System & World Scale**

The original engine operates in a discrete 3D Cartesian space using unsigned 8-bit coordinates (X, Y, Z) in the range 0..255.

* **Axes & Cardinal Directions:**  
  * **East:** \+X \| **West:** \-X  
  * **North:** \+Y \| **South:** \-Y  
  * **Up:** \+Z \| **Down:** \-Z  
* **Room Origin & Floor:**  
  * Every room is centered horizontally at (X \= 128, Y \= 128).  
  * Floor elevation room\_size\_Z is always 128 (0x80).  
* **Room Dimensions (room\_size\_tbl):**  
  * Each room has a size type (0, 1, or 2\) defining half-extents (room\_size\_X, room\_size\_Y) from center 128:  
    * **Type 0 (Square):** half\_X \= 64, half\_Y \= 64 → valid interior X ∈ \[64, 192), Y ∈ \[64, 192\)  
    * **Type 1 (Narrow E–W):** half\_X \= 32, half\_Y \= 64 → valid interior X ∈ \[96, 160), Y ∈ \[64, 192\)  
    * **Type 2 (Narrow N–S):** half\_X \= 64, half\_Y \= 32 → valid interior X ∈ \[64, 192), Y ∈ \[96, 160\)  
* **Object Bounding Box Semantics:**  
  * x, y: **Center** of the object on the horizontal plane.  
  * z: **Bottom** of the object.  
  * width: **X radius** (half-width). Extends \[x \- width, x \+ width\].  
  * depth: **Y radius** (half-depth). Extends \[y \- depth, y \+ depth\].  
  * height: **Full Z height**. Extends \[z, z \+ height\].

## **2\. Isometric Projection & Depth Sorting**

### **2.1 3D-to-2D Projection (calc\_pixel\_XY)**

The original display is 256 × 192 pixels with pixel\_Y \= 0 at the **bottom** of the screen (sprites draw upward from pixel\_Y).

GDScript  
\# Original ZX Spectrum coordinates (origin at bottom-left, Y increases upward)  
var pixel\_x: int \= (x \+ y \- 128\) \+ pixel\_x\_adj  
var pixel\_y: int \= ((y \- x \+ 128\) \>\> 1\) \+ z \- 104 \+ pixel\_y\_adj

\# Godot 2D conversion (origin at top-left, Y increases downward)  
\# Note: anchor sprite at its bottom-left corner, or subtract sprite\_height.  
var godot\_x: float \= float(pixel\_x)  
var godot\_y: float \= float(192 \- pixel\_y)

Each entity type applies a fixed (pixel\_x\_adj, pixel\_y\_adj) offset to align its sprite bitmap with its 3D hitbox (e.g., standard blocks use (-16, \-8), player human legs use (-12, \-6), player wulf legs use (-12, \-7), special objects use (-12, \-4)).

### **2.2 Topological Depth Sorting (calc\_display\_order\_and\_render)**

Knight Lore uses a pairwise 3D topological painter's algorithm rather than a simple X \+ Y sort, ensuring tall pillars, arches, and stacked blocks occlude accurately.  
For any two drawable objects A and B, compute a 3-axis ternary relation code c ∈ \[0..26\]:

> 1. **Z-axis relation (c\_z):**  
   * If A.z \>= B.z \+ B.height: c\_z \= 0 (A is above B)  
   * Else if B.z \>= A.z \+ A.height: c\_z \= 2 (A is below B)  
   * Else: c\_z \= 1 (Z-overlap)  
> 2. **Y-axis relation (c\_y):**  
   * If (A.y \- A.depth) \>= (B.y \+ B.depth): c\_y \= 0 (A is north of B)  
   * Else if (B.y \- B.depth) \>= (A.y \+ A.depth): c\_y \= 6 (A is south of B)  
   * Else: c\_y \= 3 (Y-overlap)  
> 3. **X-axis relation (c\_x):**  
   * If (A.x \- A.width) \>= (B.x \+ B.width): c\_x \= 0 (A is east of B)  
   * Else if (B.x \- B.width) \>= (A.x \+ A.width): c\_x \= 18 (A is west of B)  
   * Else: c\_x \= 9 (X-overlap)

Sum code \= c\_z \+ c\_y \+ c\_x:

* **If code in \[3, 4, 6, 7, 12, 15, 16\]:** B must be drawn **before** A (B is behind/under A). Recursively resolve B's dependencies first, tracking visited nodes in a cycle-detection list to break mutual cycles.  
* **If code \== 13 (3D intersection on all three axes):** If either A or B is a special quest object (0x60..0x66), convert that special object into sparkle sprite 187 (which destroys it).

## **3\. Core Game Loop & Object Architecture**

### **3.1 Fixed Tick Loop (onscreen\_loop)**

Implement gameplay logic in a fixed-rate tick (approx. **12–15 Hz** to match ZX Spectrum pacing; Godot \_physics\_process with an accumulator):

> 1. Increment global RNG/tick counters (seed\_2 \+= 1, seed\_3 mixed with frame entropy).  
> 2. Iterate through active objects in fixed table order (max 40 slots):  
   * **Slot 0:** Player bottom half (legs — owns physics, input, collision).  
   * **Slot 1:** Player top half (torso/head — follows Slot 0 at Z \+ 12, ignored in 3D physics).  
   * **Slots 2–3:** Special objects currently in the room (max 2; Slot 3 is dynamically occupied by cauldron bubbles in room 136).  
   * **Slots 4–39:** Room background objects (arches, walls, trees, gates, wizard, cauldron), followed by room foreground objects (blocks, enemies, hazards).  
> 3. Run pause check, cauldron bubble spawner (if in room 136), depth-sorted render, sun/moon timer update, and inventory HUD update.  
> 4. If both player slots (0 and 1\) are null, trigger lose\_life() and reload the room.

### **3.2 Entity State Flags**

Every entity maintains these core state flags:

| Flag Field | Bit | Meaning |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| flags (+7) | 7 / 6 | vflip / hflip sprite orientation |
| flags (+7) | 3 | auto\_adjust — arch doorway alignment (player only) |
| flags (+7) | 2 | moveable — can be pushed horizontally and rides moving platforms |
| flags (+7) | 1 | ignore\_3d — excluded from 3D collision checks |
| flags (+7) | 0 | near\_arch — bypasses room wall clamping to allow room exit |
| flags12 (+12) | 7..4 | entry\_counter — forced walk-in ticks when entering a room (starts at 3\) |
| flags12 (+12) | 3 | jumping — player is airborne from a jump |
| flags12 (+12) | 2 / 1 / 0 | z\_oob / y\_oob / x\_oob — hit room boundary or obstacle on that axis |
| flags13 (+13) | 7 | deadly\_if\_hits\_target — kills entity it collides into |
| flags13 (+13) | 6 | dead — entity has been killed |
| flags13 (+13) | 5 | deadly\_if\_hit\_by\_mover — kills entity that collides into it |
| flags13 (+13) | 3 | triggered — set when another object lands on top (dropping/collapsing blocks) |
| flags13 (+13) | 2 | up (bouncing ball) / dropping (spiked ball) |
| flags13 (+13) | 1 / 0 | Movement direction (north / east) or just\_dropped (special objects) |

## **4\. Physics & 3D Collision Resolution**

### **4.1 Standard Step (dec\_dZ\_and\_update\_XYZ)**

Most dynamic entities call this every tick:

> 1. Apply gravity: dZ \-= 1\.  
> 2. Run resolve\_collisions() (axis-by-axis clamping).  
> 3. Commit velocity: x \+= dX, y \+= dY, z \+= dZ.

### **4.2 Axis-by-Axis Resolution (adj\_for\_out\_of\_bounds)**

If ignore\_3d is set, skip collision resolution. Otherwise, clear x\_oob, y\_oob, z\_oob, temporarily set ignore\_3d on self, and resolve strictly in order: **Z → X → Y**.  
For each axis with non-zero velocity:

> 1. **Room Bounds Check:**  
   * **Z:** While z \+ dZ \< room\_size\_Z (128): set z\_oob, step dZ toward 0 by 1\.  
   * **X** (skipped if entry\_counter \> 0 or near\_arch is set): While abs((x \+ dX) \- 128\) \+ width \>= room\_size\_X: set x\_oob, step dX toward 0 by 1\.  
   * **Y** (skipped if entry\_counter \> 0 or near\_arch is set): While abs((y \+ dY) \- 128\) \+ depth \>= room\_size\_Y: set y\_oob, step dY toward 0 by 1\.  
> 2. **Object-to-Object Intersection Check:** Iterate through all other active objects where ignore\_3d \== false. Three-axis overlap tests:  
   * overlap\_x(A, B, dX): abs((A.x \+ dX) \- B.x) \< (A.width \+ B.width)  
   * overlap\_y(A, B, dY): abs((A.y \+ dY) \- B.y) \< (A.depth \+ B.depth)  
   * overlap\_z(A, B, dZ):

GDScript  
var dz\_diff \= (A.z \+ dZ) \- B.z  
if dz\_diff \< 0:  
    return (-dz\_diff) \< A.height  
else:  
    return dz\_diff \< B.height

* **On Collision with B:**  
  * Set the corresponding axis OOB flag on A.  
  * **Lethality:**  
    * If A.deadly\_if\_hits\_target: set B.dead \= true.  
    * If B.deadly\_if\_hit\_by\_mover: set A.dead \= true.  
  * **X/Y Collision side-effects:** If B.moveable is true, copy A.dX (or A.dY) into B.dX (or B.dY) to push B.  
  * **Z Collision side-effects:**  
    * Set B.triggered \= true (activates dropping/collapsing blocks).  
    * If A.moveable is true: if A.dX \== 0, set A.dX \= B.dX; if A.dY \== 0, set A.dY \= B.dY (allows riding moving platforms).  
  * Step A's velocity on the current axis toward 0 by 1 and re-test against B until clear or velocity reaches 0\.

## **5\. World Map & Room Transitions**

* **Map Grid:** Rooms use an 8-bit ID (0..255) representing a 16 × 16 grid (128 rooms are populated in location\_tbl).  
  * **West:** (id & 0xF0) \| ((id \- 1\) & 0x0F)  
  * **East:** (id & 0xF0) \| ((id \+ 1\) & 0x0F)  
  * **North:** (id \+ 16\) & 0xFF  
  * **South:** (id \- 16\) & 0xFF  
* **Arch Proximity & Auto-Alignment (upd\_2\_4):**  
  * Near-side arch objects compute the doorway center (arch\_x, arch\_y, arch\_z) and check player/special objects (slots 0..3) with auto\_adjust set.  
  * If within the arch's proximity box (\|dz\| \< 4, horizontal box 15×6 or 6×15), sets near\_arch \= true.  
  * If within a wider 15×15 box, applies a ±1 nudge (d\_x\_adj or d\_y\_adj) perpendicular to the walking direction to center the player in the doorway.  
* **Exiting a Room (handle\_exit\_screen):**  
  * Triggered when entry\_counter \== 0 and near\_arch \== true, and the entity crosses past the room boundary in its facing direction:  
    * West: x \+ dX \+ width \< 128 \- room\_size\_X → sets x \= 0  
    * East: x \+ dX \- width \>= 128 \+ room\_size\_X → sets x \= 255  
    * North: y \+ dY \- depth \>= 128 \+ room\_size\_Y → sets y \= 255  
    * South: y \+ dY \+ depth \< 128 \- room\_size\_Y → sets y \= 0  
  * Updates screen to the adjacent room ID and sets entry\_counter \= 3\.  
  * **Player transition:** Snapshots player state to respawn scratchpad, sets player sprites to appear-sparkles (120), saves current room's special object coordinates back to special\_objs\_tbl, loads the new room, and calls adjust\_plyr\_xyz\_for\_room\_size to place the player at the opposite doorway and match the entry arch's Z height (essential for high arches at Z \= 176 / 0xB0).  
  * **Special object transition:** Special objects pushed through an arch update their screen ID without changing the player's room.

## **6\. Player Controller, Inventory & Transformation**

### **6.1 Player Hitbox & Facing**

* **Bottom half (Slot 0):** width \= 5, depth \= 5, height \= 23, flags \= DRAW \| AUTO\_ADJUST \| MOVEABLE.  
* **Top half (Slot 1):** Copies x, y, width, depth, flags from Slot 0, height \= 0, z \= bottom.z \+ 12, ignore\_3d \= true. Randomly glances left/right for 8 ticks when seed\_3 \< 2 or seed\_3 \>= 254\.  
* **Four Facing Directions:** Derived from (hflip, graphic\_no & 8): 0 \= West, 1 \= East, 2 \= North, 3 \= South.

### **6.2 Movement & Jumping**

* **Control Schemes:**  
  * **Rotational:** Left/Right rotates facing 90° (blocked while jumping or entering a room; 2-tick turn cooldown). Forward walks in facing direction.  
  * **Directional:** Pressing a cardinal direction turns toward it if not facing it, or walks forward if already facing it.  
* **Walk Speed:** 3 units/tick along X or Y (±3), plus any ±1 arch auto-alignment adjustment. Leg animation cycles through 6 frames (0..5), settling on standing frames 2 or 4 when idle.  
* **Variable-Height Jump (handle\_jump, move\_player):**  
  * Can jump if entry\_counter \== 0, jumping \== false, and dZ \>= \-1.  
  * Sets jumping \= true, dZ \= 8\.  
  * **Gravity while jumping:** If dZ \>= 0 AND Jump is **held**, dZ \-= 1\. Otherwise (Jump released or falling dZ \< 0), dZ \-= 2\.  
  * Landing (z\_oob \== true while dZ \< 0\) clears jumping.  
  * When walking through an arch outside room bounds (chk\_plyr\_OOB fails), upward dZ is clamped to 0\.

### **6.3 Inventory & Pickup/Drop (handle\_pickup\_drop)**

* The player carries up to **3 items** in a rotating FIFO/queue (objects\_carried\[0..2\]).  
* **Preconditions:** Button must be newly pressed (debounced), player is inside room bounds, not jumping, and standing on a surface (z\_oob \== true).  
* **Headroom check:** Temporarily tests player at z \+ 12 for intersections; if blocked, sets cant\_drop \= true.  
* **Pickup:** Expands player box by (+4 width, \+4 depth, \+4 height, z \- 4\) and checks special\_objs\_here (slots 2..3) for items (graphic\_no ∈ \[0x60..0x66\]).  
  * If found: removes item from room, disables disable\_spike\_ball\_drop, inserts item at front of queue, and shifts queue down. If the queue was full (slot 2 occupied), the displaced item drops in place.  
* **Drop:** If no item was picked up and the room has an empty special-object slot (max 2 per room; max 1 in room 136 because slot 3 is reserved for cauldron bubbles):  
  * If objects\_carried\[2\] is empty, simply rotates the queue.  
  * If objects\_carried\[2\] has an item and cant\_drop \== false: spawns the item at the player's (x, y, z) (width \= 5, depth \= 5, height \= 12, flags \= DRAW \| MOVEABLE, just\_dropped \= true), **lifts the player upward by z \+= 12** (so the player stands on the dropped item), and rotates the queue.  
  * **Cauldron Drop:** In room 136, if dropped while player z \>= 152, converts item to cauldron-arc state (graphic\_no \|= 8, i.e., 104..110) and sets obj\_dropping\_into\_cauldron \= true (locks player input and applies dZ \= 2 to player until resolved).

### **6.4 Day/Night Cycle & Sabreman/Wulf Transformation**

* **Timer (print\_sun\_moon, display\_sun\_moon\_frame):**  
  * Advances 1 step every **8 game ticks** ((seed\_2 & 7\) \== 0), moving indicator X from 176 to 225 (**392 ticks per half-day**, **784 ticks per full day**).  
  * When X \== 225: toggles Sun (0x58) ↔ Moon (0x59), resets X \= 176, and sets transform\_flag \= true.  
  * Each transition back to **Sun** (dawn) increments days (BCD). Reaching **Day 40** (0x40 BCD) triggers immediate **Game Over**.  
* **Transformation (chk\_and\_init\_transform, upd\_92\_to\_95):**  
  * Triggers once entry\_counter \== 0 and jumping \== false.  
  * Freezes player for **8 animation steps** (advancing every 4 ticks, 32 ticks total), cycling random transform sprites (92..95) with alternating hflip. Player remains vulnerable to lethal hazards during transformation.  
  * On completion, flips between Human (legs 16..29, top 32..47) and Wulf (legs 48..61, top 64..79).  
* **Form-Specific Gameplay Differences:**  
  * **Bouncing Ball:** Chases Wulf; flees from Human.  
  * **Cauldron Room (136):** Cauldron bubbles reveal the next required item to Human, but turn into a lethal **Repel Spell** when Wulf is present.

## **7\. Quest Progression, Lives & Scoring**

* **New Game Initialization (main):**  
  * **Lives:** Starts with 5 total lives (displayed as 4 spare lives after initial spawn).  
  * **Starting Room:** Randomly chosen from 4 rooms: 47 (0x2F), 68 (0x44), 143 (0x8F), 179 (0xB3).  
  * **Required Cauldron Sequence (objects\_required):** 14 items (2 of each of the 7 types: 0=Diamond, 1=Poison, 2=Boot, 3=Chalice, 4=Cup, 5=Bottle, 6=Crystal Ball), base order \[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 3, 5, 0, 6, 1, 2, 4\], left-rotated by a random 4..7 positions.  
  * **Special Object Placement (special\_objs\_tbl):** 32 fixed spawn coordinates across the castle are assigned types cycling through 0..7 (0..6 \= quest items, 7 \= Extra Life idol) starting from a random offset (4 of each item exist in the world).  
* **Extra Life (upd\_103, type 7 / sprite 0x67):**  
  * Cannot be carried. Touching it (with player width \+ 1, depth \+ 1\) increments lives, clears disable\_spike\_ball\_drop, plays a sound, and deletes the idol.  
* **Cauldron Logic (Room 136):**  
  * **Bubbles (upd\_160\_to\_163):** Spawn in Slot 3 at (128, 128, 128\) when Slot 2 is empty and quest is incomplete. Rise at dZ \= 2 until Z \>= 160, then dZ \= 1\.  
    * If player is **Human**: periodically flashes the sprite of objects\_required\[objects\_put\_in\_cauldron\].  
    * If player is **Wulf**: converts into a **Repel Spell** (164..167) and enables 3D collision (ignore\_3d \= false).  
  * **Arcing Item (upd\_104\_to\_110):** Moves ±1 per tick toward (128, 128\) while staying at Z \>= 152; once centered, sets ignore\_3d \= true and drops to Z \= 128\.  
    * If (graphic\_no & 7\) \== objects\_required\[objects\_put\_in\_cauldron\]: increments objects\_put\_in\_cauldron and flashes screen colors. At 14, sets all\_objs\_in\_cauldron \= true, wipes room objects, and turns room blocks into victory sparkles (131..133) that rise to Z \>= 164 and converge on the player, triggering Victory when within 6 units of player X and Y.  
    * If wrong item: item is destroyed without credit.  
* **Death & Respawn (lose\_life):**  
  * When player.dead \== true (and all\_objs\_in\_cauldron \== false), both player halves turn into death sparkles (112..119) and clear to null.  
  * lose\_life() decrements lives (if \< 0 → Game Over), restores player from the room-entry snapshot, syncs Human/Wulf form with the current Sun/Moon state, and respawns with appear-sparkles (120..127).  
* **Quest Percentage & Rating:**  
  * Tracks visited rooms in a 256-bit bitset (scrn\_visited).  
  * percent \= round((rooms\_visited \+ 2 \* objects\_put\_in\_cauldron) / 156.0 \* 100.0)  
  * Rating index (0..7): (((rooms\_visited \- 1\) \>\> 5\) & 0x06) \| int(all\_objs\_in\_cauldron) → \["POOR", "AVERAGE", "FAIR", "GOOD", "EXCELLENT", "MARVELLOUS", "HERO", "ADVENTURER"\].

